bad fixtures:\n- `test-fixture/bad/dir-without-index/` - directory without index.md\n- `test-fixture/bad/no-frontmatter/` - index.md with invalid frontmatter\n\nLet me create all of this. I'll first create the test fixture files, then the test script.\n\nWait, let me rethink. The prompt says the test script should be at the specified path and should test things. But a Python test script can only do static checks. It can't actually run the agent and verify its behavior.\n\nLet me re-read the prompt more carefully...\n\nOK so the test script should:\n1. Verify the test fixture exists and has correct structure (fixture completeness check)\n2. Verify SKILL.md for regression (KR7)\n3. Create bad fixture directories for testing\n4. Verify files, frontmatter, etc.\n\nThis is a static test - the actual agent execution tests would be done manually by a human or an agent.\n\nLet me design the test script:\n\n```python\n#!/usr/bin/env python3\nimport json\nimport sys\nimport os\nimport re\n\ndef main():\n    errors = []\n    project_root = os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))))\n    \n    # ... tests ...\n    \n    result = {'pass': len(errors) == 0, 'errors': errors}\n    print(json.dumps(result))\n    sys.exit(0 if result['pass'] else 1)\n```\n\nThe test script path is: `/Users/xuning/IdeaProjects/skills/.rick/jobs/job_1/doing/tests/task3.py`\n\nSince the script is at `.rick/jobs/job_1/doing/tests/task3.py`, the project root would be several levels up:\n- task3.py location: `.rick/jobs/job_1/doing/tests/`\n- project root: `../../../../` i.e. `os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.abspath(__file__))))))`\n\nActually let me think about this more carefully:\n- `__file__` = `<project_root>/.rick/jobs/job_1/doing/tests/task3.py`\n- `os.path.dirname(__file__)` = `<project_root>/.rick/jobs/job_1/doing/tests`\n- `os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(__file__))` = `<project_root>/.rick/jobs/job_1/doing`\n- `os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(__file__)))` = `<project_root>/.rick/jobs/job_1`\n- `os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(__file__))))` = `<project_root>/.rick/jobs`\n- `os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(__file__)))))` = `<project_root>/.rick`\n- `os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(os.path.dirname(__file__))))))` = `<project_root>`\n\n6 levels up is messy. Let me just use `os.path.dirname(__file__)` and navigate from there.\n\nActually, let me think about what the correct number of `os.pardir` or `os.path.dirname` calls would be:\n\nFrom `.rick/jobs/job_1/doing/tests/task3.py`:\n- 1 level: `.rick/jobs/job_1/doing/tests`\n- 2 levels: `.rick/jobs/job_1/doing`\n- 3 levels: `.rick/jobs/job_1`\n- 4 levels: `.rick/jobs`\n- 5 levels: `.rick`\n- 6 levels: project root\n\nSo 6 calls to `os.path.dirname()` to get to the project root. Let me use a cleaner approach:\n\n```python\nproject_root = os.path.abspath(os.path.join(os.path.dirname(__file__), '..', '..', '..', '..', '..'))\n```\n\nThat's 5 `..` to go from `.rick/jobs/job_1/doing/tests/` to project root:\n- `..` from tests → doing\n- `..` from doing → job_1\n- `..` from job_1 → jobs\n- `..` from jobs → .rick\n- `..` from .rick → project root\n\nYes, 5 `..` to get to the project root.\n\nNow let me plan the test steps:\n\n1. **Fixture 完整性前置检查**: Check all 7 files exist with frontmatter containing 5 required fields\n2. **正常路径测试: 理解项目整体架构**: Verify that test fixture has the correct structure (index.md, services, domain, infrastructure)\n3. **正常路径测试: 追踪业务流程**: Verify flow file exists and links to related documents\n4. **正常路径测试: 概念搜索**: Verify User entity document has key attributes\n5. **边界用例: index.md 缺失**: Verify the bad fixture directory structure\n6. **边界用例: 空知识库**: Verify empty fixture\n7. **异常路径: 断链处理**: Verify broken link exists in fixture\n8. **异常路径: type-registry.md 缺失**: Verify bad fixture directory\n9. **异常路径: 格式损坏**: Verify bad frontmatter fixture\n10. **回归检查 (KR7)**: Check SKILL.md for TASK2_FILL placeholders, chapter order, content contradictions\n\nWait, actually the test is about verifying the test fixture and skill are correct. The \"test\" of the agent behavior itself can't be done in a Python script. So I should focus on what I CAN verify:\n\n1. Fixture files exist with correct structure\n2. Frontmatter is valid\n3. SKILL.md regression checks\n4. Bad fixture directories exist for manual testing\n\nBut actually, re-reading the prompt more carefully, I think the test script is meant to be a \"placeholder\" that will initially fail (RED phase of TDD), and then someone will implement the actual okf-knowledge-read skill to make it pass. So the test should assert behaviors that SHOULD work once the skill is implemented.\n\nBut wait - this is a Python test script. It can't actually run the agent skill. So what can it test?\n\nLet me re-read the \"测试质量自检\" section again:\n\n> 生成测试脚本后，**必须立即运行以下命令**：\n> ```bash\n> python3 /Users/xuning/IdeaProjects/skills/.rick/jobs/job_1/doing/tests/task3.py\n> ```\n> \n> **根据运行结果判断**：\n> - 输出 `\"pass\": false` → 符合预期，测试正确覆盖了待实现的功能\n> - 输出 `\"pass\": true` → 需要判断原因：\n>   - ✅ **可接受**：该功能已被前面的 task 顺带实现，测试通过是合理的\n>   - ❌ **需重写**：功能尚未实现但测试已通过，说明测试逻辑有缺陷（如断言过弱、检查对象错误），**必须重新编写测试脚本**\n\nSo the expected behavior is that the test should FAIL initially. The features (okf-knowledge-read) haven't been fully implemented yet, so the test SHOULD fail.\n\nNow I need to think about what types of tests will actually fail for features that haven't been implemented yet. The test-fixture also doesn't exist yet, so I need to either:\n- Create the fixture as part of the test setup\n- Or check whether the fixture exists\n\nActually, the prompt says: \"本 task 需要可用的 OKF 知识库作为测试数据。**必须使用方案 B（手动创建 fixture）**\"\n\nSo the test script should include the fixture creation? Or should the fixture be created separately?\n\nLooking at the task structure, I think the fixture should be created as part of the test setup. The test should:\n1. Create the fixture directory structure\n2. Write all necessary fixture files\n3. Then run the verification tests\n\nWait, but the prompt says the test is for \"okf-knowledge-read\" skill. The fixture is INPUT to the test. The test verifies that the okf-knowledge-read SKILL.md is correctly defined and the fixture is ready.\n\nLet me think about this differently. The \"测试方法\" section describes the testing of the agent's BEHAVIOR. But since we can't run the agent from Python, the test script will:\n\n1. Verify that the test fixture is complete and valid (prerequisite checks)\n2. Verify the SKILL.md has no issues (regression checks)\n3. For the behavioral tests, verify that the conditions are set up correctly for manual/manual agent testing\n\nActually, I think the test should focus on what's checkable. Let me re-read the test cases:\n\nLooking at the test methods:\n1. Normal path: understanding architecture - this would test the agent reads index.md, type-registry.md, matches concepts, etc.\n2. Normal path: tracing business flows - similar\n3. Normal path: concept search - similar\n4. Edge: missing index.md - test error handling\n5. Edge: empty knowledge base - test error handling\n6. Error: broken links - test error handling\n7. Error: missing type-registry.md - test fallback\n8. Error: format corruption - test error handling\n\nFor a Python test script, I can:\n- Verify fixture files exist and are valid\n- Verify SKILL.md structure\n- Create bad fixture directories\n\nFor the actual agent behavioral tests, since I can't run the agent, I should verify the preconditions are set up and check what I can statically.\n\nLet me create a comprehensive test that:\n1. Creates/verifies the test fixture\n2. Verifies all frontmatter\n3. Checks SKILL.md regression\n4. Verifies bad fixture directories\n\nLet me now create both the fixture files and the test script.\n\nActually, I need to create the test fixture files. The fixture is needed for the tests to work. Let me create them all.\n\nLet me define the fixture structure:\n\n```\nskills/okf-knowledge-read/test-fixture/\n├── index.md\n├── references/\n│   └── type-registry.md\n├── domain/\n│   └── entities/\n│       ├── user.md\n│       └── message.md\n├── services/\n│   └── im-gateway/\n│       └── overview.md\n├── flows/\n│   └── c2c-message-send.md\n├── infrastructure/\n│   └── mysql.md\n├── bad/\n│   ├── dir-without-index/\n│   │   └── (empty directory, no index.md)\n│   └── no-frontmatter/\n│       └── index.md (without frontmatter)\n```\n\nLet me create all these files now. I'll create the test script first, and the fixture as part of the test setup OR create them separately.\n\nActually, the better approach for a test script: the test should be able to CREATE the fixture if it doesn't exist (as part of test setup), and then verify everything. This way the test is self-contained.\n\nBut wait - that would make the test very long with a lot of file creation code. Let me think about the best approach...\n\nI think the cleanest approach is:\n1. Create the fixture files separately (I can do this now)\n2. The test script verifies everything and reports results\n\nBut the prompt says the fixture path is fixed to `skills/okf-knowledge-read/test-fixture/` and doesn't yet exist. So I should create it.\n\nLet me create the fixture files first, then the test script. The test script will verify the fixture and SKILL.md.\n\nLet me write the fixture files. Each needs frontmatter with: type, title, description, tags, timestamp.\n\nLet me create a plan and execute it:\n\n1. Create test-fixture directory structure\n2. Create index.md\n3. Create references/type-registry.md\n4. Create domain/entities/user.md\n5. Create domain/entities/message.md\n6. Create services/im-gateway/overview.md\n7. Create flows/c2c-message-send.md\n8. Create infrastructure/mysql.md\n9. Create bad/dir-without-index/ (empty dir)\n10. Create bad/no-frontmatter/index.md (without proper frontmatter)\n11. Create the test script\n\nLet me draft all the fixture content now.\n\nFor index.md, based on the template:\n```markdown\n# 业务领域\n\n- [User](domain/entities/user.md) - 用户实体，系统核心领域对象\n- [Message](domain/entities/message.md) - 消息实体，C2C 消息的核心载体\n\n# 服务\n\n- [IM Gateway](services/im-gateway/overview.md) - 即时通讯网关服务，负责消息路由和连接管理\n\n# 消息 / 数据流\n\n- [C2C Message Send](flows/c2c-message-send.md) - C2C 单聊消息发送完整链路\n\n# 基础设施\n\n- [MySQL](infrastructure/mysql.md) - 主数据库，存储用户、消息等核心数据\n\n# 架构决策\n\n# 引用\n```\n\nFor user.md:\n```markdown\n---\ntype: BusinessEntity\ntitle: User\ndescription: 用户实体，系统核心领域对象，代表一个注册用户\ntags: [user, domain, entity]\ntimestamp: 2026-07-19T00:00:00+08:00\n---\n\nUser 是 IM 系统中代表注册用户的核心实体。\n\n## 核心规则\n\n- 每个 User 有唯一 userId，由系统自动生成\n- 用户状态包括 ACTIVE、INACTIVE、BANNED\n- 用户名全局唯一，创建后不可修改\n\n## 关键属性\n\n| 属性 | 类型 | 说明 |\n|------|------|------|\n| userId | string | 用户唯一标识 |\n| username | string | 用户名，全局唯一 |\n| phone | string | 绑定手机号 |\n| email | string | 绑定邮箱 |\n| status | enum | 用户状态：ACTIVE/INACTIVE/BANNED |\n| createdAt | timestamp | 创建时间 |\n\n## 相关概念\n\n- User 通过 [Message](message.md) 进行 C2C 通信\n- User 通过 [IM Gateway](../services/im-gateway/overview.md) 建立长连接\n\n## Proto/接口定义\n\n```protobuf\n// user.proto\nmessage User {\n  string user_id = 1;\n  string username = 2;\n  string phone = 3;\n  string email = 4;\n  UserStatus status = 5;\n  int64 created_at = 6;\n}\n```\n\n## 引用\n\n[1] [IM 系统架构设计](https://example.com/architecture)\n```\n\nFor message.md:\n```markdown\n---\ntype: BusinessEntity\ntitle: Message\ndescription: 消息实体，C2C 单聊消息的核心载体\ntags: [message, domain, entity]\ntimestamp: 2026-07-19T00:00:00+08:00\n---\n\nMessage 是 IM 系统中单聊消息的核心实体。\n\n## 核心规则\n\n- 每条 Message 有唯一 messageId\n- 消息状态包括 SENDING、SENT、DELIVERED、READ\n- 消息内容支持 text、image、video、file 四种类型\n- 消息发送后不可修改，仅可撤回\n\n## 关键属性\n\n| 属性 | 类型 | 说明 |\n|------|------|------|\n| messageId | string | 消息唯一标识 |\n| fromUserId | string | 发送方 userId |\n| toUserId | string | 接收方 userId |\n| content | string | 消息内容 |\n| type | enum | 消息类型：TEXT/IMAGE/VIDEO/FILE |\n| status | enum | 消息状态：SENDING/SENT/DELIVERED/READ |\n| sentAt | timestamp | 发送时间 |\n\n## 相关概念\n\n- Message 由 [User](user.md) 发送和接收\n- Message 通过 [C2C Message Send](../flows/c2c-message-send.md) 流程投递\n- Message 持久化存储在 [MySQL](../infrastructure/mysql.md) 中\n\n## Proto/接口定义\n\n```protobuf\n// message.proto\nmessage Message {\n  string message_id = 1;\n  string from_user_id = 2;\n  string to_user_id = 3;\n  string content = 4;\n  MessageType type = 5;\n  MessageStatus status = 6;\n  int64 sent_at = 7;\n}\n```\n\n## 引用\n\n[1] [IM 消息系统设计](https://example.com/message-design)\n```\n\nFor services/im-gateway/overview.md:\n```markdown\n---\ntype: Service\ntitle: IM Gateway\ndescription: 即时通讯网关服务，负责客户端长连接管理、消息路由和协议转换\nresource: https://github.com/example/im-gateway\ntags: [gateway, service, im]\ntimestamp: 2026-07-19T00:00:00+08:00\n---\n\nIM Gateway 是 IM 系统的接入层网关服务，负责管理客户端长连接和消息路由。\n\n## 端口\n\n| 端口 | 协议 | 用途 |\n|------|------|------|\n| 8080 | HTTP | REST API 管理接口 |\n| 9000 | WebSocket | 客户端长连接 |\n| 9001 | gRPC | 内部服务间通信 |\n\n## 核心职责\n\n### 连接管理\n\n维护客户端 WebSocket 长连接，处理连接建立、心跳保活、断线重连。\n\n### 消息路由\n\n将客户端发来的消息路由到下游消息处理服务，并推送消息到目标客户端。\n\n### 协议转换\n\n将 WebSocket 协议转换为内部 gRPC 协议。\n\n## 关键架构决策\n\n- [ADR-001](decisions/adr-001-connection-model.md) — 选择 WebSocket 作为长连接方案\n\n## gRPC/API 接口\n\n```protobuf\n// gateway.proto\nservice IMessageway {\n  rpc SendMessage(SendMessageRequest) returns (SendMessageResponse);\n  rpc BatchPush(BatchPushRequest) returns (BatchPushResponse);\n}\n```\n\n## 依赖\n\n- [MySQL](../infrastructure/mysql.md) — 存储连接状态和离线消息\n- [User](domain/entities/user.md) — 用户身份验证\n\n## 引用\n\n[1] [IM Gateway 设计文档](https://example.com/gateway)\n```\n\nFor flows/c2c-message-send.md:\n```markdown\n---\ntype: DataFlow\ntitle: C2C Message Send\ndescription: C2C 单聊消息发送完整链路：客户端 → IM Gateway → 消息服务 → 存储 → 推送\ntags: [c2c, message, flow]\ntimestamp: 2026-07-19T00:00:00+08:00\n---\n\nC2C 单聊消息发送是 IM 系统最核心的业务链路，涉及消息的发送、存储、推送全流程。\n\n## 完整链路\n\n```\nClient(A) → IM Gateway → Message Service → MySQL(存储) → IM Gateway → Client(B)\n                                                          ↓\n                                                     Push Service\n```\n\n## 各环节职责\n\n| 环节编号 | 服务 | 关键操作 |\n|----------|------|----------|\n| 1 | IM Gateway | 接收客户端 WebSocket 消息，验证连接有效性 |\n| 2 | Message Service | 校验消息内容，生成 messageId，写入 MySQL |\n| 3 | IM Gateway | 查询目标用户连接状态，推送消息或存储为离线消息 |\n\n## 投递语义\n\n- 采用 At-Least-Once 投递语义\n- 客户端通过 messageId 去重\n- 发送失败时自动重试 3 次\n\n## 实现断言\n\n| 断言内容 | 验证状态 | 代码证据位置 |\n|----------|----------|--------------|\n| 消息写入 MySQL 后返回 messageId | 已验证 | message-service/handler.go:42 |\n| 离线消息在用户重连后批量推送 | 已验证 | im-gateway/reconnect.go:78 |\n\n## 引用\n\n[1] [IM 消息链路设计](https://example.com/message-flow)\n```\n\nFor infrastructure/mysql.md:\n```markdown\n---\ntype: Infrastructure\ntitle: MySQL\ndescription: 主数据库，存储用户、消息、会话等核心业务数据\ntags: [mysql, database, infrastructure]\ntimestamp: 2026-07-19T00:00:00+08:00\n---\n\nMySQL 在 IM 系统中承担核心数据存储职责。\n\n## 用途\n\n### 用户数据存储\n\n- **Key**: user:{userId}\n- **Value**: 用户基本信息（username, phone, email, status）\n- **Ops**: CRUD，支持按 userId、username 查询\n\n### 消息存储\n\n- **Key**: message:{messageId}\n- **Value**: 消息内容、类型、状态、发送时间\n- **Ops**: 写入、查询历史消息、更新消息状态\n\n## 数据流\n\n```\nMessage Service → INSERT message → MySQL\nQuery Service → SELECT * FROM message WHERE ... → MySQL\n```\n\n## 部署\n\n```yaml\n# docker-compose.yml\nmysql:\n  image: mysql:8.0\n  environment:\n    MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD: ${MYSQL_ROOT_PASSWORD}\n    MYSQL_DATABASE: im_db\n  ports:\n    - \"3306:3306\"\n  volumes:\n    - mysql_data:/var/lib/mysql\n```\n\n## 引用\n\n[1] [MySQL 8.0 文档](https://dev.mysql.com/doc/)\n```\n\nFor references/type-registry.md:\n```markdown\n---\ntype: Reference\ntitle: Type Registry\ndescription: 本项目使用的所有 OKF 文档 type 及其含义\nresource: skills/okf-knowledge-gen/templates/\ntags: [meta, reference]\ntimestamp: 2026-07-19T00:00:00+08:00\n---\n\n此文件定义 OKF 知识库中所有文档类型的分类标准。\n\n## Type 定义\n\n| type | 含义 | 适用场景 | frontmatter 特有字段 |\n|------|------|---------|-------------------|\n| BusinessEntity | 业务实体 | 领域模型中的核心对象 | — |\n| BusinessConcept | 业务概念 | 跨实体的通用概念 | — |\n| Service | 微服务 | 项目的每个服务模块 | resource |\n| DataFlow | 数据/消息流 | 跨服务的交互链路 | — |\n| Infrastructure | 基础设施 | 依赖的中间件 | — |\n| ArchitectureDecision | 架构决策记录 | 重要技术决策 | — |\n| Reference | 外部引用 | 客户端、部署、指南、元文档 | resource |\n\n## 使用说明\n\n- 所有文档必须在其 frontmatter 中声明 `type` 字段\n- `title` 字段必须简洁且唯一\n- `description` 字段用于索引和目录预览\n```\n\nLet me now create all these files and then the test script.","signature":"b0e3492d-a82b-4ab3-8d11-46c303a65e23"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1493,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":50432,"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5242faff-5238-48b8-bebb-13e618bb6f5e","uuid":"c4e19125-ad4a-4857-873e-2ce06fcdab3b"}
